			"Message": "style(Mist): Format README with badge header, wrapped lines, and HTML funding table\n\nReformat the README to improve readability and align with project documentation conventions across CodeEditorLand components.\n\n- Add a header badge table (Last-commit, Issues, Star, Downloads) with dark/light mode support for quick repository status at a glance\n- Wrap all long prose lines at ~80 characters for better terminal and diff readability\n- Convert Key Components and Integration tables to properly aligned markdown table syntax\n- Replace the markdown funding table with an HTML table containing proper SVG logos and descriptive alt text linked to Land, PlayForm, NLnet, and NGI0 Commons Fund\n- Update Related Documentation links from local relative paths to absolute GitHub tree URLs pointing to the Mist repository\n\nNo functional changes — presentation and maintainability only.",
			"SHA": "46c3e2d5de87e507536c854fcb9a7abdb6a6458b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T02:02:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Document all public items in Library, Resolver, WebSocket modules\n\nAdd comprehensive Rustdoc comments across three modules addressing documentation gaps identified in the nightly cargo doc build.\n\nLibrary.rs: Document the crate-level module with WebSocket Transport and Forward Security feature listings, add a Modules section enumerating each submodule's purpose, and add Links section pointing to the repository and architecture guide.\n\nResolver.rs: Document both the PascalCase New constructor (project convention) and the snake_case new alias (reqwest compatibility), clarifying when each variant should be used.\n\nWebSocket.rs: Document SharedSecret::random (thread-local RNG source), as_hex (64-char hex encoding), from_hex (error semantics for invalid input); HandlerRegistry::new (empty initial state), Register (replaces existing), Lookup (returns None for unregistered); and Client::is_closed (post-close invocation behaviour and recovery path).",
			"SHA": "50ba381d514d864772014684e9b65c33b76c4c56"
		}
